Subject: [PATCH 2/2] davsync: a 403 on the write names the folder it went to,
 and a full quota (#4927)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The error for a write the server refused, with the address's folder
listing fine, said the account couldn't write in that folder (/dav) -
but the write went to magpie's own folder inside it, and the listing
never proved anything about writing. On 坚果云 (Nutstore) the refusal
is usually the free tier's upload quota used up, which answers 403 on
a PUT with everything else fine (#4927), so the old text sent the user
to check a thing they can't check.

The error now looks at magpie's own folder first: there, the server
refused to change files in it, and the text says so and mentions the
quota; missing, the server refused to have magpie make it, and the
text says to make the folder by hand, or put an existing folder in
the address.

Fixes #4927

